      },
      "message": "docs(process): the P? label pauses an issue until the maintainer sets a priority\n\n- AGENTS.md: Pick's search excludes `label:\"P?\"`; a new rule says a P?\n  issue is held by the maintainer - never picked, claimed, researched or\n  re-prioritised by an agent, never beside a P0/P1/P2 label, and only the\n  maintainer swaps it for a real priority. Agents never file with P?.\n- README.md: the Issues section explains P? for contributors.\n- review-prs skill step 4: a contributor's claim comment on a P? issue is\n  not mirrored; one reply says the issue is paused.\n\nThe label itself is created on GitHub (lavender, \"Paused: never picked\nuntil the maintainer sets a real priority\").\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
